# No AI attribution in SCM text

Do **not** include AI attributions in any developer-facing SCM text, including:
- commit messages (title/body)
- pull request titles/bodies/descriptions/comments (when drafting)
- release notes / changelogs (when drafting)

## Disallowed examples
- "Generated by Cursor"
- "Written with ChatGPT"
- "Co-authored-by: AI"
- "Created with the help of AI"
- "Thanks to AI assistance"

## Allowed
- Purely human-authored wording focusing on intent and impact.
- Mentioning tools only when strictly necessary for technical clarity (e.g., "ran `npm run build`"), but never as authorship/credit.

